BT 1 0 0 1 0 48.9 Tm /F1 10.3 Tf 14.8 TL (Bias is error from overly simplistic assumptions \(underfitting\); variance is error from sensitivity to training) Tj T* (data fluctuations \(overfitting\). Total expected error = bias^2 + variance + irreducible noise. Increasing model) Tj T* (complexity typically lowers bias but raises variance, so the goal is to find the complexity level that minimizes) Tj T* (the sum, often via cross-validation and regularization.) Tj T* ET
